    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe de-duplication rule lives entirely in one existing function \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.service` \u2014 in a single file, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n`src/main/java/.../owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n- The step now injects `OwnerRepository` (an OfficeFloor bean-by-type parameter, same pattern as `CountNamesakes`/`RequireUniqueIdentity`).\n- It computes the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code as before, collects existing owners' `customerCode`s into a `Set`, then appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and incrementing until the code is unused. Since `assignCode` runs before `save`, the new owner isn't yet in `findAll()`, so there's no self-collision.\n\nDesign notes:\n- Kept the logic inline in the one method already responsible for the code rather than adding a helper method or a new pipeline step \u2014 that avoids paying the surrounding-class complexity again and keeps the change to **one function in one file**. The loop keeps the method's cyclomatic complexity low (a single `for` condition).\n- Updated the class Javadoc, which previously claimed \"No sequence number is used.\"\n\nThe black-box test `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` passes: distinct owners get distinct codes, and the collision path guarantees uniqueness when hashes would otherwise clash.",
